{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `_activateCube` doc says "only `/cube use` passes it" — `_cubeReload` passes it too**

The doc block states:

> [allowDegrade] is the remembered opt-in for [source]; only `/cube use` passes it, so a settings-hub selection always resets the flag and `/cube reload` can never leak a degrade into another source.

`_cubeReload` also passes the parameter explicitly (`allowDegrade: degrade`, recomputed from the remembered flag and the re-resolved backend) — it must, because omitting it would reset the flag on every reload and break the remembered-reload feature. The *intent* ("only `/cube use` introduces a fresh opt-in") is right; the letter is off, and this is exactly the invariant a future reader will want stated precisely:

```dart
/// [allowDegrade] is the remembered opt-in for [source]; a fresh opt-in
/// arrives only via `/cube use` — `/cube reload` re-passes the remembered
/// (backend-rechecked) value, and every other caller takes the default,
/// so a settings-hub selection always resets the flag.
```
